# Rust build output
/target/
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
*.dSYM/

# Cargo.lock is tracked on purpose: the version rubric treats the exercise
# toolchain and crate versions as part of the public interface, so exercises
# must stay reproducible. Do not ignore it.

# Executables from compiling a single file with `rustc` directly, e.g.
# `rustc hello_world.rs`. They land next to the source instead of under
# `target/`, and Git has no pattern for "extensionless executable", so each
# one is listed as a chapter adds it.
Chapter01/hello_world
*.exe

# Coverage and profiling data (`-C instrument-coverage`, `cargo bench`)
*.profraw
*.profdata

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editors
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Claude Code: settings.json is shared, settings.local.json is per-machine
.claude/settings.local.json
